1
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:10,480
Good morning.

2
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:12,190
Good morning. My name is Richard Stewart.

3
00:00:12,190 --> 00:00:13,880
I'm here to see Mr. Carlson.

4
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:18,030
Please  sit down,Mr.Stewart.  Mr. Carlson will be with you shortly.

5
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:22,010
Thank you.

6
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:23,290
Excuse me, Mr. Carlson,

7
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:24,590
but Richard Stewart is here

8
00:00:24,590 --> 00:00:27,550
for his ten o'clock appointment with you.

9
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:28,970
OK. Thank you.

10
00:00:28,970 --> 00:00:31,340
Like I said, he'll be with you shortly.

11
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:37,580
Thank you.

12
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:42,060
Yes, Mr. Carlson. Yes, sir.

13
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:44,110
He's ready for you, Mr. Stewart.

14
00:00:44,110 --> 00:00:46,410
Thank you. In there?

15
00:00:46,410 --> 00:00:53,770
Yes. In there. Good luck.

16
00:00:53,770 --> 00:00:58,270
Come in, come in.

17
00:00:58,270 --> 00:01:00,440
This is a crazy morning. Hello, Richard.

18
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:01,540
Hello, Mr. Carlson.

19
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:03,500
Sit down, sit down.

20
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,830
Thank you for seeing me on such short notice.

21
00:01:05,830 --> 00:01:08,140
I hope you've brought your pictures along.

22
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:13,160
I see that you have. Let's get right to it.

23
00:01:13,160 --> 00:01:15,490
We need a new coffee-table book,

24
00:01:15,490 --> 00:01:20,480
and a book of photos about the United States still feels right.

25
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:28,500
OK, let's take a look.

26
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:43,240
Good. Very good. Family Album, U.S.A.

27
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:45,800
It's an excellent title.

28
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:48,300
If you had to describe the book in one sentence,

29
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:50,360
how would you do it?

30
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:56,110
Well, I'd describe it as a book which is a ...

31
00:01:56,110 --> 00:01:58,470
a portrait of the United States--

32
00:01:58,470 --> 00:02:02,810
the places, the people--mostly the people.

33
00:02:02,810 --> 00:02:05,460
The things they do, the ways they live,

34
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:09,200
the places they visit, and the landmarks.

35
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:12,210
A photographic journey.

36
00:02:12,210 --> 00:02:13,230
These are wonderful--

37
00:02:13,230 --> 00:02:15,910
these photos in your performing arts section.

38
00:02:15,910 --> 00:02:18,410
Carnegie Hall, Lincoln Center.

39
00:02:18,410 --> 00:02:19,960
I'm glad you like them.

40
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:23,670
I do, but ...

41
00:02:23,670 --> 00:02:25,740
But?

42
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:29,930
There's something missing. You've got a good eye, Richard.

43
00:02:29,930 --> 00:02:32,910
You're a terrific photographer.

44
00:02:32,910 --> 00:02:34,830
But before I can publish your work,

45
00:02:34,830 --> 00:02:37,910
I need to meet with my marketing department,

46
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:40,930
and you've got to do one more thing.

47
00:02:40,930 --> 00:02:43,120
What's that, Mr. Carlson?

48
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,860
In the section on culture,

49
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:46,900
you've included performing arts centers,

50
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:50,640
but you've left out street performance. The mimes.

51
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:56,840
The musicians. The dancers--in the parks and on the streets.

52
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:59,820
Richard, if you go out    Richard,

53
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:01,370
and photograph street performances in the city,

54
00:03:01,370 --> 00:03:03,470
you'll have it.

55
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:06,010
That is a great idea.

56
00:03:06,010 --> 00:03:09,370
The performing arts centers and the street performances.

57
00:03:09,370 --> 00:03:10,680
I'll do it.

58
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:14,360
If you do it, I'll publish your work.

59
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,620
Are you serious?

60
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:17,450
I've never been more serious.

61
00:03:17,450 --> 00:03:21,930
When do you think you can return with street performances?

62
00:03:21,930 --> 00:03:24,100
A couple of weeks.

63
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:28,480
If they're as good as the rest of these pictures, it's a deal.

64
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:34,990
You won't be disappointed, Mr. Carlson. Thanks.

65
00:03:34,990 --> 00:03:37,440
Good-bye, Richard, and good luck. See you in two weeks.

66
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:43,610
Good-bye, Mr. Carlson. Thanks.

67
00:03:43,610 --> 00:03:47,620
So if you like the street-performance photos,

68
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:50,470
you'll really publish Family Album, U.S.A.?

69
00:03:50,470 --> 00:03:53,460
When I say something, I mean it.

70
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:55,300
Go to work. Good-bye.

71
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:58,300
Good-bye.
